From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob McSwain <jacob@mcswain.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:10:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): a relayed WebSocket ends with a close frame,
 not a cut

gateway.restart_listener_relay_close_sockets (false = off): with restart_listener_relay_seconds, a WebSocket the old listener relays byte for byte that is still open when the relay window ends gets a close frame with code 1012 (service restart), sent between two of the successor's frames, instead of a cut connection (EOF). Its client reconnects at once, now straight to the successor. Other relayed connections end as before.
